-- title:
--   Specialising the Tate reading of j(mathsf q^{qℓ'd}) to cyclic quotients
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q \ge 5$, $M'$ is a non-zero natural number not divisible by $q$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the valuation subring of the number field $k_0$ obtained by pulling $A$ back, once $k_0$ is introduced below.
--
--   *Supersingular places and the constant reduction.* A finite set $W$ of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` $= \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ over the residue field of $A$ is given, and `hW` says that membership in $W$ is equivalent to membership in `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M' (ResidueField A)`; an element $s$ of $W$ is fixed. The hypothesis `hle` requires the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ (the Laurent base change of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`) to be contained in `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over $A$: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places, compatibility of the integers and of the residue with $A$ and with $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, the scaling property that every non-zero element becomes an integer with non-zero residue after multiplication by a constant, preservation of place degrees, and compatibility of divisors with the place map. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that $R_0$ computes the coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under the coefficientwise map induced by $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$.
--
--   *The arithmetic model.* An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ are given, together with the hypotheses that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), that its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every element $a$ of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element $c$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   *The auxiliary prime and the $q$-expansion field.* A prime $\ell'$ is fixed with $\ell' \ne q$, $\ell' \ge 3$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$, together with an element $\xi$ of $k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`) and admits a ring embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ carrying it to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$ (`hιξ`). The field $K$ is an intermediate field of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ which, by `hK`, is the Laurent base change to $k_0$ of `xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ') ^ 2 * M') (levelH (q * ℓ') M')`, the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/(q\ell'))^\times$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$. The element $j$ of $K$ is, by `hj`, the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under the coefficientwise embedding $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q)) \to k_0((\mathsf q))$, and $j$ is non-zero.
--
--   *Functoriality and Drinfeld data over $A_0$.* The hypothesis `hℓ` asserts that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData`, the predicate `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ'` (the two marked points satisfy the affine equation, the $\ell'$-division polynomial `preΨ` vanishes at their $x$-coordinates, and both independence elements are units) is carried to `IsLevelPStructure (C • W) ℓ'` of the transported data. The hypothesis `hM` asserts likewise that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (which is `W.IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k = 2$ and `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise) is carried by a variable change $C$ to `IsGamma0PowAt (C • W) p k` of `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`. Group laws $\mathcal G$ over $A_0$ are given, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`) and to have the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`), together with a level transport $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport` (`h𝒯`). Finally `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms on the graded rings `projModelGradingCR` realising variable changes (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and coefficient changes along $A_0$-algebra maps (`IsCoefficientHom`), each with the irrelevant ideal of the target dominated by the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source. These data enter the rigid Weierstrass datum $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the product of the $\Gamma_0$-power component at $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ component and the Drinfeld level-$q$ component.
--
--   *The moduli package and the Tate point.* $P_0$ is an absolute level moduli package for $\mathcal R$: a ring $B_0$ over $A_0$ with a universal point `P₀.univ` of $\mathcal R$ such that every point of $\mathcal R$ over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0 \to T$; `P₀.classify` picks out that map. A point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ is given whose $j$-invariant, read in $k_0((\mathsf q))$, is `jqNModC k₀ (q * ℓ')`, the $\mathsf q^{q\ell'}$-expansion of $j$ (`hx₀`). The map `clC` is an $A_0$-algebra map from $B_0$ to `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A_0[j]$, and `hclC` says that `clC` followed by the inclusion into $K$ is `P₀.classify x₀`.
--
--   *The Tate model of $x_0$ (`hμ`).* This hypothesis asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and of a raw representative $r$ of the rigid datum over $K$ such that: (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) writing $(\mathfrak x, \mathfrak y) :=$ `cuspPoint k₀ (q * ℓ') ξ ![1, 0]` for the unit associated with $\xi$, one has $C.u \cdot (2\mathfrak x + 1/6) = 2\mathfrak y + \mathfrak x$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$ and $C.t = 1/24$ (constants as Hahn series); (iii) the curve of $r$, base changed along $K \hookrightarrow k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals $C \bullet$ `tateBase k₀ (q * ℓ')`; (iv) for every prime $p$ dividing $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta$ in $F'$, the $\Gamma_0$-power kernel polynomial `r.level.1 p`, base changed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and then mapped coefficientwise by $f$, equals `kernelVariableChangeDeg` of $C$ (mapped by $f$) in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)` applied to $\prod_{a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\, F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^a)_1)$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; (v) the level-$\ell'$ part `r.level.2.1`, base changed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, equals the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData k₀ (q * ℓ') ξ ![q, 0] ![0, -q]` (the vectors taken in $\mathbb Z/(q\ell')$); (vi) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y$ in $K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ are the four coordinates `xP`, `yP`, `xQ`, `yQ` of the variable change by $C$ of `cuspData k₀ (q * ℓ') ξ ![ℓ', 0] ![0, -ℓ']`, and such that the Drinfeld sections `r.level.2.2.P` and `r.level.2.2.Q` pass through $(P_x, P_y)$ and $(Q_x, Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   *Conclusion.* Under these hypotheses, for every non-zero natural number $d$ dividing $M'$, every witness `hcK` that `jqNModC k₀ (q * ℓ' * d)` lies in $K$, and every $c$ in $B_0$ with `P₀.classify x₀ c` equal to that element of $K$, the following holds. Assume the Tate reading `hread`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ which is an $A_0$-algebra and a $K$-algebra with the two structures compatible, every raw point $x_\Omega$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\Omega$ whose class is the image of $x_0$ under the structural map $K \to \Omega$, and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Omega$ satisfying the generator condition that the additive order of $g$ is $M'$ and that for every prime $p \mid M'$, every $n$ and every non-singular affine point $(x_1, y_1)$ with $n \cdot g = (x_1, y_1)$ and $n \cdot g$ of order $p^{v_p(M')}$ the value $x_1$ is a root of `xΩ.level.1 p`, one has
--   $$\mathrm{algebraMap}\,K\,\Omega\,(j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'd})) = \mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x_\Omega.\mathrm{curve})\,\langle (M'/d)\cdot g\rangle\,d,$$
--   where `cyclicQuotientJ V H N` is $c_4^3/\Delta$ of `V.cyclicQuotientCurve H N` and $\langle\,\cdot\,\rangle$ denotes the subgroup of integer multiples. Then for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ which is an $A_0$-algebra, every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : B_0 \to \Omega$ annihilating every $b'$ with `clC b' = 0` (`hφ`), with $M'$ invertible in $\Omega$ in the sense that its image is non-zero (`hM'Ω`), every raw point $x_\Omega$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\Omega$ whose class is the image of `P₀.univ` under $\varphi$ (`hxΩ`), and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Omega$ satisfying the same generator condition (`hg`):
--   $$\varphi(c) = \mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\,(x_\Omega.\mathrm{curve})\,\langle (M'/d)\cdot g\rangle\,d.$$
--
--   This is the specialisation step in the moduli-theoretic reading of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-type level structure near the Tate curve: an identity between a classifying coordinate and the $j$-invariant of a cyclic quotient, known over the $q$-expansion field from the Tate model, is transported to an arbitrary algebraically closed point of the classifying ring compatible with the integral chart. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_classify_preimage_forall_apply_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_etale_of_tatePoint_gamma0Pow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_classify_preimage_forall_apply_eq_cyclicQuotientJ_etale_of_tatePoint_gamma0Pow), which produces a classify-preimage with this property at all such points.
